            <ArticleTitle>Scleroderma en coup de sabre with central nervous system involvement.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>486-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a patient with scleroderma en coup de sabre and central nervous system symptoms. She presented with a linear scleroderma on her left paramedian forehead and scalp and suffered from headaches and dizziness. Axial T2-weighted MRI showed a 1 cm, high intense signal abnormality in the medial aspect of the left frontal lobe.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
